    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0061" n="53" xml:id="pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/851</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-18">July 18, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador called at his request. I remarked to him that in making a
                    record of opposition to the closing of the Burma road at the instance of Japan,
                    I did not quite expect a furore in Great Britain, and added that of course our
                    chief purpose was to direct attention to the lawless conduct of Japan. The
                    Ambassador seemed perfectly satisfied about what we had done, without expressly
                    or specifically saying so.</p>
                <closer><signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ull</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
